<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
<title>Perfils: Generate topographic profiles</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>
<body>
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

  <p>A graph in MMM format is
  automatically generated with the following elements: the profile itself,
  labels, mesh, boxes with titles,etc, that users may later edit or adapt
  according to their own preferences.<br/>
  It should be noted that the itinerary cannot be just any ARC vector: it must
  not have forks or stops in its route. There are, however, no limits to the
  number of vertices or to the complexity of its associated database.</p>

  <p>On the X axis, the profile generated represents the distance (planimetric
  or on the ground, as indicated) in relation to the origin of the itinerary.
  The Y axis represents the height of the itinerary. This height is obtained
  from the ARC vector and/or from the Digital Elevation Model, generating all the additional vertices
  necessary in the itinerary. This ensures optimum incorporation of the
  altimetric information from the DEM.</p>

  <p>The application makes it possible to generate the graphic representation
  based on the calculation of a series of parameters: number of axis
  divisions, multiples, maximums and minimums, etc, automatically or it allows
  the user to set some of these parameters. Symbolization of the different
  graphic elements is totally automatic. However, the user can configure
  colors, thicknesses, fonts, etc according to his or her own criteria in the
  same way as for any other type of cartographic layer.<br/>
  For example, the colour of the graphic line is automatically defined as
  constant, but with the symbolization options it is possible to make a
  relation between a field of the database and a palette.</p>

  <p>Despite the fact that <b>Perfils</b> is an application that is designed
  fundamentally for a topographic profile, it can also be used to generate the
  profile of any other variable. For example, temperature instead of height,
  if we have its continuous model (and digital terrain model - DTM).</p>
  <hr/>

  <exclusiva>
